# The one problem fragment for the merged arclight-soc2-audit-cycle domain
# (Stage 2 Fortune-5 rescale; domain object renamed from "solace" to
# "arclight" — see packs/soc2-audit-pack/templates/arclight-case-study.ttl.tmpl
# for the case-study rationale). Init holds ONLY the Phase 1 (Scoping &
# System Description) entry atom;
# the goal is ONLY the terminal Phase 10 (Auditor Report Handoff)
# deliverable (1 conjunct — the merged goal stays far inside
# PDDL8_MAX_CONJUNCTS=8 because no other fragment declares a goal). Every
# intermediate phase is forced by the precondition chain, never by goal
# conjuncts: that is how the 8-constraint budget splits across 10 phases
# without ever concentrating in one conjunction.
#
# COMPLIANCE-OVERCLAIM FENCE: the goal atom is "evidence-bundle-complete",
# never "compliant" or "opinion-issued" — per the fence disclosed in
# packs/soc2-audit-pack/ontology.ttl, this pipeline's terminal deliverable
# is an evidence bundle for a human auditor's professional judgment, never
# a compliance verdict.
@prefix ceng:    <urn:chatman:engine#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

_:artifact
    skos:notation "SOC2-CYCLE-PROBLEM" ;
    dcterms:description "Full SOC2 audit engagement cycle problem: from audit-engaged to evidence-bundle-complete through all 10 chained phases."@en ;
    ceng:pddlProblem """
(define (problem arclight-soc2-audit-cycle-p)
  (:domain arclight-soc2-audit-cycle)
  (:objects arclight)
  (:init (audit-engaged arclight))
  (:goal (evidence-bundle-complete arclight)))
""" .
